  "question_text": "Silver and copper are mixed in the ratios 2:5 and 4:7 to prepare two alloys A and B. Equal\nquantities of these alloys A and B are mixed to prepare a third alloy C. The ratio of silver\nand copper in C is\n2:5 4:7 A B \nA, B \nC C ",
